		{
			"id": "019cc64c-1a32-70fe-a132-8832639dc877",
			"title": "Understanding Suffering with Quranic Wisdom",
			"hook": "Suffering directed towards Allah",
			"summary": "This series, a collaboration between Dr. Ali and MuslimMatters, addresses adolescent grief by drawing on Quranic wisdom. It highlights that adolescent grief differs neurologically and developmentally from adult grief, impacting emotional regulation and worldview construction. The text uses the Quranic narratives of Prophet Yaqub ﷺ and Prophet Musa ﷺ with Khidr ﷺ to illustrate how to direct suffering toward Allah, not away from Him. It emphasizes that patience (sabr) involves turning to Allah at the first strike of calamity, not suppressing emotions. The series also outlines warning signs for professional support and offers guidance on what to say and not say to grieving teenagers.",
			"summaryProvider": "gemini",
			"summaryStatus": "verified",
			"topic": "ethics",
			"sourceUrl": "https://muslimmatters.org/2026/03/06/why-do-bad-things-happen-to-good-people-night-18-with-the-quran/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=why-do-bad-things-happen-to-good-people-night-18-with-the-quran",
