		{
			"id": "019cc64c-5471-7301-991a-16e16fa21d5a",
			"title": "Understanding Depression in Islamic Context",
			"hook": "Suffering does not equate to spiritual failure",
			"summary": "Depression is a medical condition involving neurological changes, not a lack of faith, and requires professional treatment. The Islamic tradition, as taught by the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ, explicitly encourages seeking medical treatment for all illnesses, including mental health conditions. Prophet Ayyub's ﷺ story illustrates that suffering does not equate to spiritual failure, as Allah tested him despite his righteousness. Differentiating between spiritual struggle and clinical depression is crucial, as the latter necessitates clinical evaluation and support alongside spiritual care.",
