		{
			"id": "019cc132-3e47-71f6-8c05-bb39770f4bac",
			"title": "Understanding Spiritual Dryness in Worship",
			"hook": "Consistency is highly valued by Allah",
			"summary": "Spiritual dryness, the absence of feeling during worship, is a common human experience, not a sign of weak faith. The Prophet Muhammad ﷺ addressed this, explaining that spiritual highs and lows are natural. He ﷺ told Handhalah that while intense spiritual states are possible, \"there is a time for this and a time for that.\" This means consistency in worship, even without feeling, is highly valued by Allah. Parents are advised to offer support and understanding rather than increasing religious demands, which can be counterproductive.",
