		{
			"id": "019cc131-c2cf-73e1-80e5-bc21145b30f7",
			"title": "Ramadan in Canada: Community Outreach",
			"hook": "Knowing one another through shared iftar",
			"summary": "Ramadan in Canada, where Muslims are a minority, offers a unique opportunity for community outreach. The Qur'an states, \"O mankind, We created you from a male and a female and made you peoples and tribes so that you may know one another\" (49:13). This principle is exemplified through various iftars: a hospital event fostering spiritual care understanding, a Parliament Hill gathering bridging political divides, a City Hall initiative with public Ramadan lights, and an intimate living room gathering supporting women escaping domestic abuse. These occasions highlight how sharing iftar allows for mutual understanding and living Islamic values within Canadian society.",
