			"id": "019cc12e-fdcd-701f-9f76-300ddfb04a17",
			"title": "Talaq Said In Anger",
			"hook": "Talaq in anger is still valid",
			"summary": "Q: Does a divorce said in anger count as a valid divorce if a husband says it three times without intending divorce? A: According to Islamic scholars, including Ibn 'Abidin in Radd al-Muhtar, if a husband says divorce three times while sane and aware, the divorce is valid, regardless of his emotional state or intent, unless he was unconscious or had medical issues, and it would be considered sinful to stay with him, thus consulting with knowledgeable scholars is recommended for guidance.",
