		{
			"id": "019cc132-ac4c-75f9-8f63-0979b8343a6c",
			"title": "Ramadan's Gentle Lessons",
			"hook": "Ramadan as a mirror to self",
			"summary": "As a child, I barrelled through its gates headfirst, shrieking with laughter at my big brother's suhoor antics. As a teen, I entered its gates more mindfully, resolving to read a juz a day, along with the English translation. In my twenties, I saw Ramadan as a mirror that showed me where I was and where I needed to go. Then, just like that, Ramadan came upon me as a new wife in a new land. Another Ramadan taught me hard lessons on moderation, intuition, and respecting my body's limits.",
