			"id": "019cb6e2-470a-771b-bae7-4d3c3e8ad811",
			"title": "Staying Healthy During Ramadan",
			"hook": "Fasting and weakened immune systems",
			"summary": "During Ramadan, individuals may be more susceptible to cold and flu viruses due to weakened immune systems from fasting. Colds and flu can be debilitating, causing symptoms such as a runny nose, headaches, and coughs. The influenza virus causes flu, while over 200 different viruses can cause colds, spreading through coughed and sneezed globules. Doctors often rely on the body's natural mechanisms to fight these infections, as antiviral medication may not be effective in treating them.",
