			"title": "Ramadan's Last 10 Nights",
			"hook": "The reward is more than a thousand months",
			"summary": "Allah ﷻ says in the Quran: The Night of Decree is better than a thousand months. Muhammad ﷺ used to tighten his waist belt and pray the whole night during the last ten days of Ramadan. Abu Hurayrah relates that Muhammad ﷺ said: \"Whoever spends the night of Lailat Al-Qadr in prayer out of faith and in the hope of reward, his previous sins will be forgiven.\" To maximize the last 10 nights of Ramadan, consider remaining in I'tikaf, worshiping all nights, giving charity, and eating light. A possible worship routine includes praying Maghrib, Isha', and Taraweeh, reciting the Quran, and making dua, with the goal of catching the blessed night of Laylatul Qadr, which can bring rewards equivalent to over 83 years of worship.",
