			"title": "Dua for Protection from Affliction",
			"hook": "Seeking refuge from evil judgment",
			"summary": "Muhammad ﷺ taught a supplication for protection from affliction, hardship, evil judgment, and enemies' malicious rejoicing. The dua, \"Oh Allah, I seek refuge in You from the difficulty of affliction, from the burden of hardship, from evil judgment, and from the enemy's malicious rejoicing,\" has a broad application, including protection from Muslims who harbor ill feelings. The term \"enemy\" refers to anyone who holds ill will or delights in another's misfortune, regardless of their religion. This supplication is a way to seek Allah's protection, maintaining dignity and focusing on His refuge rather than judging others' intentions.",
