			"title": "Toxic Relationships in the Quran",
			"hook": "Nuh's son refused the ark",
			"summary": "The Quran addresses toxic relationships through the story of Nuh and his son. Nuh ﷺ preached for 950 years, but his greatest pain was his son's refusal to board the ark, prompting Allah to say, \"He is not of your family. He is of unrighteous conduct\" (Surat Hud 11:46). This teaches that even the purest love has limits and one cannot force someone to be saved. Warning signs of toxic relationships include isolation, mood changes tied to one person, changed values, excessive guilt and self-blame, and fear of ending the relationship.",
